//
// Gate E cell: a function answering a vector through a `match` whose arms are a recursive call and
// literals: the first pass renamed its buffer onto the call's work ref (`__ref_1`), so each
// literal arm is copied into it and its store freed, and each arm keeps its own type (the literal
// arm the store it minted).  A subject held from a call keeps its first-pass borrow.
// @FR-M-Expr: the selected arm — a recursive call or a literal — is the match's value ([4,5]).
// @FR-F-Ret: the vector answered through the recursion is independent.
// Prints: [4,5]

enum N {
  Leaf { v: integer },
  Span { inner: N }
}
fn deps(n: N) -> vector<integer> {
  match n {
    Span { inner } => deps(inner),
    Leaf { v } => [v, v + 1],
    _ => []
  }
}
fn main() { println("{deps(Span { inner: Leaf { v: 4 } })}"); }
